      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With a recent update, it is now possible to hide printed photos from the Comfort and Safety menu. However, I still believe this should be added as a camera option.  \n\nHaving to open a large menu and change the setting every time we take a group photo is extremely inconvenient. Additionally, there is a risk of forgetting to revert the setting, which could interfere with communication.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-20T14:09:54.580Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, when taking group photos in VRChat, printed photos often get captured in the frame, sometimes obscuring someone's face or disrupting the composition of the picture. This has become a recurring issue during photo sessions.\n\nI strongly believe there should be an option to make printed photos invisible to the camera, and this feature should be enabled by default. Allowing users to toggle this visibility would provide flexibility while ensuring a smoother experience for group photo-taking without unnecessary interruptions.\n\nThank you for considering this improvement!",
